            "review_text": "Wim D\nTurin, Italy8 contributions\n0\nNice discovery next to Dang Anh hotel\nMay 2016 • Solo\nFirst time I ate Bánh cuốn. It's kind of a rolled cake made from a steamed (fermented) rice batter. It's stuffed with minced pork and mushrooms. They serve it with a fish sauce to which you need to add some lemon and/or hot pepper.\nVery friendly staff, even if I was not able to speak a single word of Vietnamese, they did their best to help me.\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nWritten May 28, 2016",
